From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:13:18 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 41/59] Plutonium: file pickers for tabs ask the shell

EXO-TAB-FEATURES (docs/features/TAB_FEATURES.md, "File pickers"): every
picker a registry tab opens goes to the shell, as a "fileChooser" tab
request. Until now the default delegate cancelled every <input type=file>.

- Tab::RunFileChooser() and EnumerateDirectory() call FileSelectHelper,
  as BrowserWebContentsDelegate does.
- In shell mode, PlutoniumSelectFileDialogFactory wraps the Files app's
  factory. For a picker whose ChromeSelectFilePolicy names a registry tab
  (inputs, the File System Access pickers, a download's Save As), it makes
  a dialog that sends {mode, upload, title, origin, filters, currentFilter,
  currentName, currentFolder, defaultExtension} and takes {paths, filter?}
  or null. Agents may answer too. If no shell takes it, or the shell that
  took it goes away, the Files app's picker opens instead.
- ChromeSelectFilePolicy::GetSourceContents() tells the factory which page
  a picker is for.
- FileSelectHelper doesn't cancel a registry tab's picker when the tab
  gets too small: a shell that reloads drops the tab's embed, and the
  picker falls back to the Files app. A hidden tab's picker is still
  cancelled (WebContentsImpl::RunFileChooser), as in Chrome.
